-- title:
--   Tame descent of crossing thickness: mw → m after completion
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a Noetherian local commutative ring and $C$ a commutative $O$-algebra which is a domain, module-finite and faithful over $O$, and let $\mathfrak n$ be a maximal ideal of $C$ lying over the maximal ideal of $O$. Let $W_2$ be a complete discrete valuation ring (a domain, discretely valued, adically complete for its maximal ideal) and $\pi \in W_2$ irreducible, and let $m, w$ be positive integers whose images in $W_2$ are units. Let $G$ be a finite group acting faithfully on $C$ by ring automorphisms commuting with the $O$-action, with $\mathrm{Algebra.IsInvariant}\ O\ C\ G$; assume the inertia subgroup $\mathfrak n.\mathrm{inertia}\ G$, regarded inside the stabiliser of $\mathfrak n$ in $G$, has cardinality $w$, that $\mathfrak n.\mathrm{inertia}\ G$ is cyclic, and that $(C/\mathfrak n)$ is separable over $O/\mathfrak m_O$. Assume given a ring isomorphism $e_O$ from the $\mathfrak m_O$-adic completion of $O$ onto $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\ W_2$ modulo the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - \pi^{mw}$. Let $S$ be a local $C$-algebra which is the localisation of $C$ at $\mathfrak n$, also an $O$-algebra compatibly, such that the completion of $S$ at its maximal ideal is an integrally closed domain, and such that $S$ is unramified over $O$ at every non-maximal prime of $S$. Then there exist a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : W_2 \to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W = (\sigma\pi)$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the completion of $S$ at its maximal ideal onto $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\ W$ modulo $(X_0X_1 - (\sigma\pi)^m)$, such that for all $o \in O$ and $w_0 \in W_2$ with $e_O(o)$ the class of the constant $w_0$, the image of $o$ in the completion of $S$ is sent by $e$ to the class of the constant $\sigma(w_0)$.
--
--   This is the tame local form of Abhyankar's lemma for an ordinary double point: a point of a finite tame Galois cover lying over a crossing of thickness $mw$, with inertia of order $w$, has completed local ring a crossing of thickness $m$ over the unramified coefficient extension, compatibly with constants. It is used by [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_uvCrossingModel_pow_of_isInvariant_of_isLocalization_atPrime`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_uvCrossingModel_pow_of_isInvariant_of_isLocalization_atPrime) in the analysis of the local structure of modular curves at the cusps and supersingular crossing points.
